  <title id="bdlsingularfreeenergy-title">Free energy of a regular and a singular two-parameter model</title>
  <desc id="bdlsingularfreeenergy-desc">The negative log marginal likelihood F of two models with two parameters and a uniform prior on the square from minus 1 to 1, plotted against the base-10 logarithm of the sample size n from 10 to 100 million. For the regular model, with K equal to a squared plus b squared over 2, F grows like the natural logarithm of n, as the Bayesian information criterion predicts for two parameters. For the singular model, with K equal to the square of a times b over 2, F grows much more slowly, like one half of the natural logarithm of n minus a log log n correction.</desc>
